suggestions.sketch:
Create a new class, e.g. ReportCoordinator, that receives OrderRepository and EmailClient. Move order_count() and mail_summary() there. ReportView keeps only presentation methods (title, describe_customer) and holds a reference to ReportCoordinator for data retrieval when needed.

```python
class ReportCoordinator:
    def __init__(self, repository: OrderRepository, mailer: EmailClient) -> None:
        self._repository = repository
        self._mailer = mailer

    def order_count(self) -> int:
        return self._repository.count()

    def mail_summary(self, address: str) -> dict[str, str]:
        return self._mailer.send(address, f"{self._repository.count()} orders")
```

Update ReportView to accept a ReportCoordinator (or keep the repository for formatting only) and delegate the two methods.
```python
class ReportView:
    def __init__(self, coordinator: ReportCoordinator) -> None:
        self._coordinator = coordinator
        self._width = 40
    # title and describe_customer stay unchanged
    def order_count(self) -> int:
        return self._coordinator.order_count()
    def mail_summary(self, address: str) -> dict[str, str]:
        return self._coordinator.mail_summary(address)
```

